  "recommendations": [
    {
      "priority": "P1",
      "issue": "Elite stops inside attack range even if its line of sight is obstructed.",
      "fix": "Treat a blocked shot as requiring locomotion. Enter windup only when both range and sight are satisfied. Do not continue idle at the line-of-sight rejection."
    },
    {
      "priority": "P2",
      "issue": "Local goal tangent has no global route or progress invariant.",
      "fix": "Keep existing crowd separation as local steering. Add a static-world route planner using inflated obstacles per radius class. A visibility graph with 16 exterior samples per obstacle (+4 world units clearance), bounds-safe edges, deterministic A*/Dijkstra and a capped waypoint list is sufficient for 4–5 circular obstacles. Replan only after goal displacement or a bounded stall timeout, with a per-tick planning cap; no render-driven state or gameplay RNG."
    },
    {
      "priority": "P2",
      "issue": "Circle projection followed by boundary clamping can return a center that overlaps a circle.",
      "fix": "Validate the final point after all constraints. Use bounded resolution and fall back to the last legal substep when projection cannot satisfy both circle and world bounds; never return a known illegal center. Add legal-start regression along the south side of lung alveolus-d."
    },
    {
      "priority": "Design",
      "issue": "Endless has a larger traversable world but peripheral space lacks competing objectives.",
      "fix": "Spawn rings follow the player, while repair and pulse anchors remain central. After navigation correctness, rotate a bounded temporary supply/counter objective into reachable outer regions so movement pays off, without forcing an exhausting perimeter sweep."
    }
  ]
